          "context": "## What was asked\n\nPublish to npm and PyPI.\n\n## What changed, and why\n\n- **Release 0.3.1.** Every protocol package moves to 0.3.1 together, as\n  `scripts/check-versions.mjs` requires: the npm coordinator, MCP and A2A\n  packages, `create-chap-app`, the Python coordinator and the five bridges,\n  with the templates' pins, the MCP registry entry, the container image, the\n  citation, the conformance Action's default ref, the reference servers and\n  the lock file. The packages on npm and PyPI are at 0.3.0, and the\n  templates pin the coordinators, so they move with `create-chap-app`. The\n  changelog's Unreleased section becomes 0.3.1, with no breaking change.\n  `create-chap-app` ships its licence and runs its tests before it\n  publishes.\n- **chap-analytics 0.2.2.** Its fix for reading the TypeScript coordinator's\n  store is released. The templates' analytics script needs it, says so in\n  its install line, and stops with that message when an older version is\n  installed.\n\n## How it was tested\n\n- `check:versions`, `check:catalogue`, `check:error-codes`,\n  `check:schemas`, `check:mcp-schemas` and `check:explorer`: all pass.\n- Build and typecheck of the three TypeScript packages; their suites: the\n  coordinator (483), MCP (34) and A2A (14), all pass.\n- The Python coordinator's suite (618) against its built 0.3.1 wheel, and\n  chap-analytics (723 pass, 2 skipped): all pass.\n- Every template generated and tested: code gate, MCP gate, production,\n  support desk and outbound approval. The code gate's analytics test passes\n  with chap-analytics 0.2.2 and stops, as intended, with 0.2.1.\n- `npm pack` of each npm package (licence and README in each), and the\n  `create-chap-app` tarball installed and run outside the repository: it\n  generates a code gate with its `.gitignore` and `.github`.\n- All seven Python projects build an sdist and a wheel, and all fourteen\n  pass `twine check`; the bridges require `chap-coordinator>=0.3.1`